# Coding Standards

Next.js 15 App Router, TypeScript (`strict`), Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui (new-york). Hosted on Vercel with Neon Postgres.

## Project layout

| Area | Location |
|------|----------|
| Routes | `app/(admin)`, `app/(public)`, `app/(customer)` |
| **Reads** (SELECT) | `lib/data/<domain>-data.ts` |
| **Writes** (mutations) | `lib/actions/<domain>-actions.ts` |
| Legacy server code | `app/lib/*-data.ts`, `app/lib/*-actions.ts` (migrate to `lib/` when touched) |
| Shared UI | `app/ui/`, shadcn primitives in `components/ui/` |
| Types | `types/definitions.ts` and domain files |
| Constants | `lib/consts/` |
| DB client | `lib/db.ts` — **only** place that creates `postgres()` |

Follow the read/write split in `lib-read-write.mdc`. New features use `lib/data/` + `lib/actions/`. New components go in `components/`.

## Components

- **Server Components by default.** Add `'use client'` only for hooks, browser APIs, or interactivity.
- **Pages** are async Server Components; fetch data via `lib/data/*`, pass props to child components.
- **Forms**: `useActionState` + server action; export a `*FormState` type with `errors`, `message`, `success`.
- **UI**: shadcn components from `@/components/ui/*`, icons from `lucide-react`, `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`.
- **Naming**: kebab-case files (`broadcast-email-form.tsx`), PascalCase exported components.

## Variable naming

Prefer **full, descriptive names** — readability over brevity.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const courseTitle = courses[0].title;
const validatedFields = CourseSchema.safeParse(data);
const selectedRegistrants = registrants.filter(r => r.isActive);

// ❌ AVOID (when a clearer name is available)
const t = courses[0].title;
const vf = CourseSchema.safeParse(data);
const sel = registrants.filter(r => r.isActive);
```

**Exceptions are fine** when the meaning is obvious from context:

- Loop indices: `index`, `i` in short loops
- Universal shorthand: `id`, `url`, `error`
- Destructuring from well-known shapes: `{ params }`, `{ success }`
- Callback params in trivial one-liners: `.map(r => r.email)`

When in doubt, use the full name.

## Server actions & validation

```typescript
'use server';

import { z } from 'zod';
import sql from '@/lib/db';
import { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache';

const Schema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(3, { message: 'El título debe tener al menos 3 caracteres.' }),
});

export type FormState = {
  errors?: { title?: string[] };
  message?: string | null;
  success?: boolean;
};
```

- Validate with Zod `safeParse`; return field errors, never throw for validation failures.
- User-facing messages in **Spanish** (es-AR for public content).
- Call `revalidatePath` after mutations; use `redirect` when navigating away after success.

## Database

- Reads live in `lib/data/`; writes in `lib/actions/`. Pages do not call `sql` directly.
- Tagged template queries via `sql` from `@/lib/db` — never instantiate `postgres()` elsewhere.
- DB columns are `snake_case`; alias to `camelCase` in SELECT: `start_date as "startDate"`.
- Filter soft-deletes: `deleted_at IS NULL` where applicable.
- Type results inline or with generics: `sql<Registrant[]>\`...\``.

## Next.js patterns

```typescript
type PageProps = { params: Promise<{ id: string }> };

export default async function Page({ params }: PageProps) {
  const { id } = await params;
  // ...
}
```